<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mostly firmer, Dow edges back.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mostly firmer, Dow edges back.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>NZ ADRs were trading with a firmer tone in late New York trade. By 8.15 a.m. NZT the Dow was off 18.54 points at 7,274.21.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company		   Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail   N.Y.    untraded</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28	     -0 1/4 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$31 3/8	 +0 3/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	 N.Y.    US$22 5/8	 +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13 7/8	 +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$36 7/8	 -0 1/4 *</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  39 1/4	     nil</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  untraded</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col London  162		 +1 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  150		 -1</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.09	    nil</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.67	     +1</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  A$2.05	     -8</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of eight shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
